s_accepted` | User ticked the terms and conditions checkbox | — |\ndocs/EVENTS.md:15:| `registration_continue_tapped` | User tapped Continue on the registration screen | `amount` (int), `terms` (bool) |\ndocs/EVENTS.md:16:| `offers_scrolled` | User scrolled the offers list | `offset` (double, how far they scrolled) |\ndocs/EVENTS.md:17:\ndocs/EVENTS.md:18:Notes\ndocs/EVENTS.md:19:- Do not send the email or the phone number as properties (PII).\ndocs/EVENTS.md:20:- Screen views are already tracked automatically, no event needed for those.\ndocs/EVENTS.md:21:- The funnel is: email started → phone started → amount changed → terms\ndocs/EVENTS.md:22:  accepted → continue tapped → offers scrolled.\nlib/screens/registration_screen.dart:1:import 'package:flutter/material.dart';\nlib/screens/registration_screen.dart:2:\nlib/screens/registration_screen.dart:3:class RegistrationScreen extends StatefulWidget {\nlib/screens/registration_screen.dart:4:  const RegistrationScreen({super.key});\nlib/screens/registration_screen.dart:5:\nlib/screens/registration_screen.dart:6:  @override\nlib/screens/registration_screen.dart:7:  State<RegistrationScreen> createState() => _RegistrationScreenState();\nlib/screens/registration_screen.dart:8:}\nlib/screens/registration_screen.dart:9:\nlib/screens/registration_screen.dart:10:class _RegistrationScreenState extends State<RegistrationScreen> {\nlib/screens/registration_screen.dart:11:  final _email = TextEditingController();\nlib/screens/registration_screen.dart:12:  final _phone = TextEditingController();\nlib/screens/registration_screen.dart:13:  double _amount = 50000;\nlib/screens/registration_screen.dart:14:  bool _terms = false;\nlib/screens/registration_screen.dart:15:\nlib/screens/registration_screen.dart:16:  @override\nlib/screens/registration_screen.dart:17:  void dispose() {\nlib/screens/registration_screen.dart:18:    _email.dispose();\nlib/screens/registration_screen.dart:19:    _phone.dispose();\nlib/screens/registration_scree